1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,980
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:03,980 --> 00:00:05,400
don't accept that.

4
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:07,750
I've carried mail
for twenty-six years.

5
00:00:07,750 --> 00:00:08,690
Walking my route

6
00:00:08,690 --> 00:00:10,710
in rain, snow and heat,

7
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:12,940
up and down
porch steps and curbs,

8
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,190
in and out of
the mail truck

9
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:16,060
with a heavy bag
on my shoulder.

10
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:16,900
That's a lot of years

11
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,470
on a pair of knees.

12
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:19,470
I had my right knee

13
00:00:19,470 --> 00:00:21,300
replaced two years ago.

14
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:24,130
It has hurt every day
since.

15
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:25,670
Not surgery pain.

16
00:00:25,670 --> 00:00:27,080
I know what that felt
like,

17
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,320
and it went away.

18
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,540
This is different.

19
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:30,370
Tight.

20
00:00:30,370 --> 00:00:31,470
Full.

21
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:32,400
Like a band around

22
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,250
the joint that never
loosens.

23
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:35,070
And for two years

24
00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,930
I've been told the same
thing.

25
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:38,070
Give it time.

26
00:00:38,070 --> 00:00:40,140
At six weeks it was
swelling,

27
00:00:40,140 --> 00:00:41,500
and swelling is normal.

28
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,260
At three months,

29
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,430
give it six.

30
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:44,430
At six months,

31
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:46,290
some knees take a full
year.

32
00:00:46,290 --> 00:00:47,030
At a year,

33
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:48,640
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

34
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:49,830
And I didn't just wait.

35
00:00:49,830 --> 00:00:51,110
We went down the list.

36
00:00:51,110 --> 00:00:52,700
More physical therapy.

37
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:53,950
Every session,

38
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:56,110
every exercise at home.

39
00:00:56,110 --> 00:00:57,320
I got stronger.

40
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:58,880
The tightness never moved.

41
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,190
The pain pills helped,

42
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:01,380
and that was the problem.

43
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:03,450
I'm already on enough
every morning,

44
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:04,370
and nobody could tell me

45
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:05,730
when I'd get to stop.

46
00:01:05,730 --> 00:01:07,030
Then a nerve block.

47
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:09,140
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

48
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,610
And after that, a second

49
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:11,620
operation to go back

50
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:13,410
in and do it over.

51
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:14,540
I said no.

52
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:15,840
Every morning I laced up

53
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,940
my work shoes

54
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:18,290
and my knee felt like a band

55
00:01:18,290 --> 00:01:19,550
was wrapped around it,

56
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:22,140
tightening every inch
I tried to straighten.

57
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:23,990
Every morning I took
something for it

58
00:01:23,990 --> 00:01:25,590
and headed out
on my route.

59
00:01:25,590 --> 00:01:26,670
Couldn't do the stairs,

60
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:28,040
couldn't stand at the
counter

61
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:29,620
long enough to finish
dinner,

62
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:31,130
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

63
00:01:31,130 --> 00:01:33,730
game without shifting
every two minutes.

64
00:01:33,730 --> 00:01:35,090
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:37,680
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,860
like getting in the car

67
00:01:38,860 --> 00:01:40,390
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:40,390 --> 00:01:41,700
into a decision.

69
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:42,870
After a long and serious

70
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:44,110
talk with my husband,

71
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:45,920
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:46,930
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:46,930 --> 00:01:48,590
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:50,680
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:54,090
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:54,090 --> 00:01:56,520
No loosening, no
infection,

77
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:57,770
nothing wrong.

78
00:01:57,770 --> 00:01:59,110
Only this time there

79
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:00,720
was no new number.

80
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,550
Nobody said

81
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:03,480
give it another six
months.

82
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:05,340
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:05,340 --> 00:02:06,250
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:07,630
lot for a while.

85
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:09,550
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:11,370
Then explain this.

87
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:13,460
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,200
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:17,460
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:19,640
I'd walked my whole route
that day.

91
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,560
Everyone in the house was
asleep

92
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,290
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

93
00:02:23,290 --> 00:02:24,300
with my leg up,

94
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,920
trying to find any angle
where

95
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:27,100
it didn't feel like
something

96
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,380
was wrapped around my knee

97
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:29,820
and tightening.

98
00:02:29,820 --> 00:02:32,320
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

99
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:34,760
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

100
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,800
And I just thought,

101
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:37,430
is this really my life
now?

102
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:39,180
I can't live like this.

103
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:41,100
So I made myself a
promise.

104
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:41,920
I wouldn't go a day

105
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:43,660
without looking for an
answer.

106
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:44,500
And when I found one,

107
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:45,500
I'd share it with everyone

108
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,910
going through the same
thing.

109
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:47,820
So I got my laptop

110
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:49,050
out and went looking.

111
00:02:49,050 --> 00:02:50,580
Not for a product.

112
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:51,900
For an explanation.

113
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,440
Mayo Clinic forums,

114
00:02:53,440 --> 00:02:55,580
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

115
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:58,450
doctor videos, medical
animations.

116
00:02:58,450 --> 00:02:59,300
And that's when I found

117
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:00,950
a video from a physical
therapist

118
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:01,600
named Dr.

119
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:04,030
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

120
00:03:04,030 --> 00:03:05,980
had been through exactly
this.

121
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:07,760
But before I say anything
else,

122
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:09,620
I want to be straight with
you.

123
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,960
You've already had
something work fast.

124
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:12,860
The ice.

125
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:14,310
The first week of a new
pill.

126
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,970
The good day after a
session.

127
00:03:15,970 --> 00:03:17,260
Then it wore off.

128
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,520
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

129
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:21,840
Fast relief isn't relief.

130
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:22,810
It's a preview.

131
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:23,900
So I'm not going to tell

132
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,060
you this works fast.

133
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:26,020
It doesn't.

134
00:03:26,020 --> 00:03:27,770
But if you're willing to
be patient,

135
00:03:27,770 --> 00:03:28,560
and to look at what's

136
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,120
going on around your new
knee

137
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:31,560
instead of inside it,
there

138
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:33,700
is a real reason it still
hurts.

139
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,820
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:37,590
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:37,590 --> 00:03:38,800
because this is what
changed

142
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,270
everything for me.

143
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:41,950
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:43,480
A knee replacement takes
out

145
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:45,170
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

146
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:46,710
in metal and plastic.

147
00:03:46,710 --> 00:03:48,560
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

148
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:50,360
you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,940
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,840
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:56,230
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:56,980
He said,

153
00:03:56,980 --> 00:03:58,300
think about a swollen foot

154
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,260
inside a shoe.

155
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,840
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:02,600
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:04:02,600 --> 00:04:04,120
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,840
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:05,840 --> 00:04:06,790
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:06,790 --> 00:04:08,290
in a limited space with
living

161
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,230
tissue packed all around
it.

162
00:04:10,230 --> 00:04:11,820
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

163
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:13,720
had to work through that
tissue.

164
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:17,020
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:19,300
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,310
But in some people that
swelling can

167
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:24,210
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

168
00:04:24,210 --> 00:04:25,840
And swollen tissue takes
up more

169
00:04:25,840 --> 00:04:27,700
room than calm tissue
does.

170
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,660
So when you bend,

171
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:31,570
that tissue gets
compressed.

172
00:04:31,570 --> 00:04:32,710
When you straighten,

173
00:04:32,710 --> 00:04:34,330
it gets pulled tight.

174
00:04:34,330 --> 00:04:35,670
That's the band.

175
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:38,010
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

176
00:04:38,010 --> 00:04:38,910
And you start being

177
00:04:38,910 --> 00:04:40,070
the one who says,

178
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:41,380
you go ahead.

179
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:42,690
I'll stay here.

180
00:04:42,690 --> 00:04:44,470
And that's exactly why so
much

181
00:04:44,470 --> 00:04:46,830
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

182
00:04:46,830 --> 00:04:48,780
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

183
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:49,830
around the knee.

184
00:04:49,830 --> 00:04:50,880
Worth doing,

185
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,120
and I'd done it.

186
00:04:52,120 --> 00:04:53,420
It does nothing about
tissue

187
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,870
taking up room.

188
00:04:54,870 --> 00:04:56,000
A nerve block quiets

189
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,950
the nerve carrying the
signal.

190
00:04:57,950 --> 00:05:00,690
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

191
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:02,260
But when that irritated
tissue

192
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,840
finally calms down,

193
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,370
it holds less fluid,

194
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:07,420
and it takes up less room.

195
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:08,910
Less room taken up means

196
00:05:08,910 --> 00:05:11,060
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

197
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:13,330
That's what takes the
pressure off.

198
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:14,830
After two years of this,

199
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:16,800
it finally made sense.

200
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,720
The problem was never the
new knee.

201
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,970
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

202
00:05:20,970 --> 00:05:22,650
He calls it the squeeze.

203
00:05:22,650 --> 00:05:25,930
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

204
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,690
I'd bought knee sleeves,

205
00:05:27,690 --> 00:05:30,350
compression braces,
creams,

206
00:05:30,350 --> 00:05:32,020
half of Amazon really,

207
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,500
and all any of it gave me

208
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,610
was an hour.

209
00:05:34,610 --> 00:05:35,570
I even looked at going

210
00:05:35,570 --> 00:05:37,590
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

211
00:05:37,590 --> 00:05:39,560
But at $200 a session

212
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,720
with nothing covered by
insurance,

213
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,150
that was a quick no.

214
00:05:43,150 --> 00:05:44,170
Then one night I went

215
00:05:44,170 --> 00:05:45,390
back to that knee
replacement

216
00:05:45,390 --> 00:05:47,350
group and actually read
it.

217
00:05:47,350 --> 00:05:48,730
Thousands of people,

218
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:50,320
years out from surgery,

219
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,350
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

220
00:05:52,350 --> 00:05:53,920
nobody could explain.

221
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,690
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

222
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:57,440
the same thing kept coming
up.

223
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:58,850
This one device,

224
00:05:58,850 --> 00:06:00,280
and people saying it was
the first

225
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:01,780
thing that made a
difference.

226
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:03,700
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

227
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,160
alright, here it comes,

228
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,400
she's selling me
something,

229
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,440
let me shut that down
right now.

230
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,090
I'm only here because I
made myself

231
00:06:10,090 --> 00:06:12,150
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

232
00:06:12,150 --> 00:06:13,110
that if I ever found

233
00:06:13,110 --> 00:06:14,420
something that helped,

234
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:16,130
I'd say so.

235
00:06:16,130 --> 00:06:17,670
It's called the KenRelief
Red

236
00:06:17,670 --> 00:06:19,550
Light Therapy Wrap.

237
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:21,860
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

238
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:22,890
It looked like the cheap

239
00:06:22,890 --> 00:06:24,100
knee sleeves off Amazon

240
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,720
that did nothing for me.

241
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,510
But I went to their
website anyway,

242
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:28,290
just to see what all

243
00:06:28,290 --> 00:06:29,510
the fuss was about.

244
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:31,120
It's the same red light
therapy

245
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:33,230
clinics charge $200 a
session

246
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:35,000
for, off machines that
cost

247
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,350
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:36,350 --> 00:06:37,210
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:37,210 --> 00:06:39,030
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:39,030 --> 00:06:40,750
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:42,980
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:42,980 --> 00:06:45,330
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:47,890
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:47,890 --> 00:06:49,490
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:49,490 --> 00:06:51,420
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:06:51,420 --> 00:06:53,820
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:55,030
Ninety days.

258
00:06:55,030 --> 00:06:57,230
Results or your money
back,

259
00:06:57,230 --> 00:06:59,730
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:06:59,730 --> 00:07:01,760
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:01,760 --> 00:07:03,780
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:03,780 --> 00:07:05,430
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,900
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:08,350
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:08,350 --> 00:07:09,820
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,590
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:12,590 --> 00:07:14,960
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:16,850
and I'd done it for two
years.

269
00:07:16,850 --> 00:07:19,110
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:19,110 --> 00:07:20,310
When it came,

271
00:07:20,310 --> 00:07:23,270
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:24,590
because I'd been let down
too

273
00:07:24,590 --> 00:07:26,710
many times to get excited.

274
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:28,840
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,870
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,750
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,980
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:34,980 --> 00:07:36,180
And that was it.

279
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:37,990
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:37,990 --> 00:07:39,190
When I took it off,

281
00:07:39,190 --> 00:07:40,390
I'll be honest,

282
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:42,210
nothing dramatic had
happened.

283
00:07:42,210 --> 00:07:44,100
And after what that video
said,

284
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,380
that's exactly what I
expected.

285
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:47,380
What was different

286
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,240
was that for the first

287
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,410
time in two years

288
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:51,140
I'd done something for my
knee

289
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,790
instead of to it.

290
00:07:52,790 --> 00:07:53,600
Twenty minutes,

291
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,920
in my own chair.

292
00:07:54,920 --> 00:07:56,740
No drive, no copay.

293
00:07:56,740 --> 00:07:58,340
They say twenty minutes.

294
00:07:58,340 --> 00:07:59,460
I did thirty,

295
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:00,580
twice a day,

296
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:02,660
lowest setting that first
week.

297
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,530
I put it on the calendar.

298
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:05,670
The first week,

299
00:08:05,670 --> 00:08:06,540
I couldn't have told

300
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,080
you if anything was
happening.

301
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:08,980
I tried not to get

302
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,210
my hopes up.

303
00:08:10,210 --> 00:08:11,940
I'd had things help for a
week

304
00:08:11,940 --> 00:08:13,160
and then stop.

305
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:15,040
But somewhere in the
second week

306
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:16,210
I noticed I'd come down

307
00:08:16,210 --> 00:08:18,490
the stairs without holding
the rail.

308
00:08:18,490 --> 00:08:19,960
I hadn't decided to.

309
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:22,180
I just did it,

310
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:23,720
then stopped halfway down

311
00:08:23,720 --> 00:08:25,100
because I realized.

312
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:26,500
By the end of the fourth
week

313
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:27,560
I'd slept through the
night

314
00:08:27,560 --> 00:08:29,200
four times running.

315
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:30,360
I stood at the counter

316
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,560
and finished making dinner

317
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,020
without looking for the
stool.

318
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,610
None of that is dramatic.

319
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:35,440
All of it was gone

320
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,700
for two years.

321
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:38,980
A few weeks later my
husband asked

322
00:08:38,980 --> 00:08:39,870
if I wanted to walk

323
00:08:39,870 --> 00:08:41,610
the long way around the
block.

324
00:08:41,610 --> 00:08:42,470
And for the first time

325
00:08:42,470 --> 00:08:43,130
in two years,

326
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,460
I said yes.

327
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:46,050
I wanted to understand
why,

328
00:08:46,050 --> 00:08:47,400
so I read the whole thing.

329
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,580
It comes down to four
steps.

330
00:08:49,580 --> 00:08:50,370
One.

331
00:08:50,370 --> 00:08:51,890
The tissue around a new
knee can

332
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:55,130
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

333
00:08:55,130 --> 00:08:55,880
Two.

334
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:58,350
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

335
00:08:58,350 --> 00:08:59,320
so it takes up more

336
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,990
room than it should.

337
00:09:00,990 --> 00:09:01,700
Three.

338
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:03,470
There's only so much room
in there.

339
00:09:03,470 --> 00:09:04,970
Bending compresses it.

340
00:09:04,970 --> 00:09:06,790
Straightening pulls it
tight.

341
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:08,400
That's the squeeze.

342
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:09,600
Four.

343
00:09:09,600 --> 00:09:11,510
Red and near-infrared
light have been

344
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:13,750
studied for calming that
inflammation,

345
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:15,090
so the swelling and the
pressure

346
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:16,490
can come down with it.

347
00:09:16,490 --> 00:09:18,100
In a randomized trial,

348
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,920
patients given light
therapy after

349
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:20,830
a knee replacement

350
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:22,030
had less pain,

351
00:09:22,030 --> 00:09:22,940
less swelling

352
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:24,300
and better early movement
than

353
00:09:24,300 --> 00:09:25,900
those who weren't.

354
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:28,520
A 2025 review said the
same,

355
00:09:28,520 --> 00:09:30,150
and was clear the evidence

356
00:09:30,150 --> 00:09:31,460
is still limited.

357
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:33,510
I probably sound like
a broken record

358
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,730
to the people
I work with

359
00:09:34,730 --> 00:09:36,140
at the post office.

360
00:09:36,140 --> 00:09:37,870
But after two years of
doing everything

361
00:09:37,870 --> 00:09:39,690
I was told and getting
nowhere,

362
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:40,770
you have no idea what it's

363
00:09:40,770 --> 00:09:42,220
like to sleep through the
night,

364
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,610
say yes to the walk,

365
00:09:43,610 --> 00:09:45,220
and get my life back.

366
00:09:45,220 --> 00:09:46,660
So take it from me.

367
00:09:46,660 --> 00:09:48,040
Don't spend another year
waiting

368
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:49,140
for it to settle.

369
00:09:49,140 --> 00:09:51,310
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

370
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,800
More than ten thousand
people

371
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,950
with pain after a knee

372
00:09:53,950 --> 00:09:56,350
replacement have already
tried this.

373
00:09:56,350 --> 00:09:58,210
Some had it worse than I
did.

374
00:09:58,210 --> 00:09:59,520
You can get the KenRelief

375
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:00,980
wrap from their website,

376
00:10:00,980 --> 00:10:02,040
with a discount link

377
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:04,560
and ninety days to try it.

378
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:06,140
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

379
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:07,350
you get your money back

380
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:08,830
and you keep the wrap.

381
00:10:08,830 --> 00:10:10,110
They only release so many

382
00:10:10,110 --> 00:10:11,150
at that price.

383
00:10:11,150 --> 00:10:12,360
If it's still there,

384
00:10:12,360 --> 00:10:13,270
get one,

385
00:10:13,270 --> 00:10:14,669
and stop the squeeze.
